# Authority of the Consuls: "Creatures your opponents control enter tapped" (CR 614.1c) and "Whenever a creature an opponent
# controls enters, you gain 1 life". CR 614.12: whether the replacement applies is judged on the permanent as it would exist
# on the battlefield, "taking into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the permanent". Under
# Bot1's Life and Limb ("All Forests and all Saprolings are 1/1 green Saproling creatures and Forest lands in addition to
# their other types") a Forest would be a creature there, so Bot2's Forest, played on turn 4, enters tapped, and Bot1 gains
# 1 life as it enters. Bot2's Plains, played on turn 2, is no creature and enters untapped (the positive control), gaining
# nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Authority of the Consuls
Life and Limb
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Forest
Island x18

